  C24 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C24\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G23 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G23\naudspec is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G24 [shape=box label="G24\nActor compJah of application c_rasta,\nrequired SIL 3: the deployment meets the\narchitectural preconditions that the\ncatalog states for SIL 3."];
  C25 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C25\ncompJah is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 1, implemented at SIL\n3."];
  G25 [shape=box label="G25\nEvery copy of compJah and of its channel_b\nis implemented at SIL 3 or above and runs\non a core provisioned to at least that\nlevel."];
  Sn8 [shape=circle label="Sn8\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of compJah is\nimplemented at or above its required SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  Sn9 [shape=circle label="Sn9\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of compJah's channel_b\nis implemented at or above its required\nSIL and runs on a core provisioned to at\nleast that level."];
  C26 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C26\nComponents introduced by\ntwo_of_two_high_sil for compJah: channel_b\non core 7 at SIL 3."];
  S10 [shape=parallelogram label="S10\nArgument by application of the\ntwo_of_two_high_sil safety architecture\npattern, over each of its general\nscenarios."];
  C27 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C27\nPattern two_of_two_high_sil [koopman, Two\nChannel (2-of-2)]: Two channels, both at\nhigh SIL, compute the same function and\nmust agree. Channel b receives the owner's\nresult, compares it with its own, and\nreturns the verdict to the owner over an\nedge with one initial token; on a\ndisagreement the owner marks its output\ninvalid and the pair goes to its safe\nstate (fails silent), so the fault\nreaction starts within one iteration. No\nexplicit voter: 2-of-2 requires agreement\nrather than a majority, so the comparison\nfolds into channel b and the owner --\nwhich is why this pattern is reachable in\nPhase 4 while NVP is not. The name is\nKoopman's; it is not IEC 61508 MooN\nnotation. Both channels always fire and\nalways produce, per the token-preservation\nobligation. A detected disagreement marks\nthe token invalid; it never withholds it.\nSo the timing guarantee holds in the\ndegraded mode too (Q4), at the price of\nbeing conservative in the fault-free case.\nAttainable SIL [3, 4]; covers random_hw,\nsystematic_sw; fails silent; voter folded."];
  G26 [shape=box label="G26\nA fault in either channel is detected as a\ndisagreement between the two channels.\n[two_of_two_high_sil/SC1]"];
  S11 [shape=parallelogram label="S11\nAchieved through the Comparison tactic\n(Checking): Detection of discrepancies of\nredundant system outputs."];
  C28 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C28\nComparison: Tests whether the outputs of\nfully redundant subsystems are equal in\norder to detect failures. Usually implies\nthe use of a redundancy tactic."];
  C29 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C29\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.3 comparator; IEC 61508-7\nA.6.5 input comparison/voting"];
  G27 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G27\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Comparison\nis implemented in compJah, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
